{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/32","id":5230578255,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVkT2ec8AAAABN8RKTw","html_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/32","diff_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/32.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/32.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/issues/32","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/32/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/32/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/issues/32/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/statuses/ccd3c701eea7747e3065294e19d09d2fd1fc659d","number":32,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add the domain types, interfaces and time limit","user":{"login":"Vijay021212","id":240779358,"node_id":"U_kgDODloAXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240779358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212","html_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #2\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds `domain.py`: the immutable types passed between the review stages (design 2.1), the `GitHub` and `ChatModel` interfaces, and `Deadline` for the hard time limit. The same types will validate the model's answers (FR-9), and the interfaces let every stage be tested with fakes (NFR-8).\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `src/pr_review_agent/domain.py` | The design 2.1 types as frozen Pydantic models (`frozen=True`, `extra=\"forbid\"`, tuples for collections); enums for the fixed value lists (state, file status, category, review level, severity, finding status, skip reason, recommendation, explore stop); validation rules; `PullRequestRef.parse()` for pull request links; `Deadline`; `ModelReply`; the `ChatModel` and `GitHub` protocols; `SetupError`, `ReviewIncomplete` and `TimeLimitReached` |\n| `src/pr_review_agent/__init__.py` | Exports the result types and the two public exceptions (design 12.1) |\n| `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock` | `pydantic` as the first runtime dependency; Pydantic's mypy plugin, so model arguments are type-checked |\n| `tests/test_domain.py` | 90 tests: every validation rule with valid and invalid input, immutability, link parsing, `Deadline` with a fake clock, the interfaces, and the dependency rule |\n| `tests/builders.py`, `tests/__init__.py` | Builders for valid sample objects, shared by later test files |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | Entry for this change |\n\n## Self-review ([plan 3.2](https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/blob/main/docs/plan.md#32-self-review-before-every-pull-request))\n\n**Gaps:** every type in design 2.1 exists, plus the small types they're built from (`DiffLine`, `LinkedIssue`, `SkippedFile`, `ToolCall`, `Excerpt`, `DroppedFinding`, `StageTiming`). Two choices beyond the design text, both following from the requirements: bug-type findings must have the trigger, current and expected behaviour (FR-9 \"every bug finding states...\"), and only the \"too large\" skip counts as a gap (FR-3 says the other skips don't). `ChangedFile.diff_available` records when GitHub leaves a diff out, so such a file can be skipped with a reason instead of being treated as empty (NFR-10). The `GitHub` interface starts with reading a pull request, which is all v0.1.0 uses; the issues that need more add their methods (snapshot #14, publishing #19, earlier comments #25, rules file #26), so the interface never lists a method that nothing implements.\n\n**Integration:** nothing uses these types yet; every later module builds on them. `__init__.py` exports the public names from design 12.1 that exist so far (`review_pull_request` and `Settings` arrive with #12 and #3).\n\n**Code quality:** ruff and strict mypy clean, now with Pydantic's mypy plugin. Each type has a docstring that says what it's for; comments explain the non-obvious choices (why unknown fields are rejected, why `diff_available` exists, which skips are gaps).\n\n## Tests ([plan 3.1](https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/blob/main/docs/plan.md#31-three-levels-of-tests))\n\n- **Unit:** valid and invalid input for each rule: line numbers matching the diff line's kind, renamed files needing their old path, the 40-character SHA, review level 1–5, blank text, unknown categories and severities, the missing failure fields on each bug-type category (including blank text), the empty reasons of a recommendation, negative timings and token counts. Also: a finding read from model-style JSON (with `\"12\"` as a string), immutability, unknown fields, link parsing (7 accepted forms, 7 rejected), `Deadline` before and after expiry with a fake clock, the interfaces with minimal fakes, and a test that fails if `domain.py` ever imports something other than the standard library and Pydantic. Coverage of `domain.py`: 100%.\n- **Integration:** not needed yet: there are no stages to wire together. The first integration test comes with the pipeline (#12).\n- **Real run:** not applicable: nothing a user sees has changed.\n\n## Definition of done ([plan 3.3](https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/blob/main/docs/plan.md#33-definition-of-done))\n\n- [x] The \"Done when\" in the issue is met\n- [x] Unit tests cover the new behaviour, including edge cases and failures\n- [x] Integration tests updated if a stage or its wiring changed (not applicable)\n- [x] Real run done and pasted, if the user-visible behaviour changed (not applicable)\n- [x] `ruff`, `mypy`, `pytest` and the coverage gate pass, locally and in CI\n- [x] Self-review written above\n- [x] Docs updated if behaviour changed (changelog)\n","labels":[{"id":12973246866,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVkT2ec8AAAADBUQJkg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/labels/feature","name":"feature","description":"New capability","color":"a2eeef","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12973251562,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVkT2ec8AAAADBUQb6g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/labels/pipeline","name":"pipeline","description":"Stages and the pipeline that runs them","color":"006b75","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T20:21:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T20:21:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a1c081559a76c4e5b7ec1c7103495de22af91cb3","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Vijay021212:2-domain-types","ref":"2-domain-types","repo":{"id":1447360121,"node_id":"R_kgDOVkT2eQ","name":"pr-review-agent","full_name":"Vijay021212/pr-review-agent","owner":{"login":"Vijay021212","id":240779358,"node_id":"U_kgDODloAXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240779358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212","html_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay